    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Castleconnell is a picturesque riverside village on the River Shannon, situated on the Limerick–Clare border and just 15km from Limerick City. Steeped in history, the village takes its name from the Castle of Connell, the ruins of which stand overlooking the Shannon. The village offers a wonderful range of local amenities, including cafés, pubs, restaurants, a national school, church, post office, Garda station, neighbourhood centre and train station. Its beautiful riverside setting provides an abundance of recreational opportunities, from fishing and rowing to scenic walks along the Shannon and through the nearby Fairy Woods.\r\n\r\nCastleconnell is renowned for its natural beauty and wildlife, including the swans that migrate from Iceland each winter. The village is also home to the Castle Oaks Hotel, Castleconnell Rowing Club and is adjacent to the  highly successful Ahane Hurling Club, giving the community a vibrant and active atmosphere.\r\n\r\nWith excellent transport links to Limerick City, Nenagh and Dublin, Castleconnell offers the perfect balance of village living, natural surroundings and easy access to major employment, education and transport hubs.\r\n\r\nThis family home is superbly positioned adjacent to Castleconnell School and Train Station. It enjoys a highly convenient setting on the approach to the village. Offering generous accommodation, lovely mature gardens and excellent potential for modernisation, the property also benefits from a spacious driveway extending around to the rear and a detached shed. \r\n\r\nCastleconnell village and its range of amenities are all within a short stroll.\r\n\r\nAccommondation comprises entrance hallway, 2 living room, kitchen, utility/wc, back porch, 3 bedrooms and shower room."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hallway - 5.01m x 2.065m\r\nAccessed from the side of the property, the entrance hallway provides a welcoming introduction to the home, with carpeted flooring and stairs leading to the first floor.\r\n\r\nLiving Room 3.05m x 4.82m\r\nLocated to the right of the hallway, this bright reception room overlooks the front garden and features a fireplace and two front-facing windows.\r\n\r\nFamily Room 3.13m x 3.53m\r\nPositioned alongside the living room, this comfortable room also enjoys a front aspect, with two windows overlooking the garden and also has a fireplace.\r\n\r\nKitchen 5.96m x 3.59m\r\nSituated at the end of the hallway, the kitchen is a generous, bright space with excellent views over the rear garden. It has ample storage space.\r\n\r\nUtility / Guest WC - 3.03m x 1.99m\r\nLocated off the kitchen, providing useful additional space.\r\n\r\nRear Porch - 2.08m x 3.08m\r\nA porch off the kitchen provides direct access to the rear garden and also houses access to the boiler room. This porch is used as the main access to the house at present.\r\n\r\nBoiler Room - 1.42m x 2.51m\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\nShower Room - 2.46m x 1.53m\r\nA modern, fully tiled shower room is located on the first floor return.\r\n\r\nLanding\r\nThe bright first-floor landing benefits from a window overlooking the side and rear of the house, there is a hotpress and Stira access to the attic.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 - 3.64m x 2.14m\r\nA well-proportioned bedroom with a pleasant front aspect.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 - 4.79m x 3.05m\r\nA generous double bedroom overlooking the front garden.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 - 3.53m x 3.52m\r\nA well-sized bedroom enjoying a rear aspect overlooking the garden.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all this home has to offer and its excellent potential."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Spacious mature front and rear gardens.\r\nSet back from the roadway on a private site\r\nOil fired central heating\r\nWithin walking distance of the village\r\nAdjacent to the school and train station"
      },
